  "contentRevision": "0.1.0",
  "notes": "Four classes, four things an author can say with the stats that decide whether a blow lands. The duellist is precise and evasive: five points of skill carry the bow's ninety to ninety-five in its hands, and four of evasion take four off anything swung at it. The fortunate authors luck alone, which is the one stat that helps whichever half of a fight its owner is in — it adds to the strikes they make and subtracts from the strikes made at them. The adept authors magic, which reaches the board only through a magical cast: max(1, magic + power - resistance). The plain authors none of the four, and that is the point of it being here — at zero every number is the number it was before these stats existed, so a class written against the old schema is not a class that plays differently. The adept's growth block names all ten stats in the one order a level-up rolls them, with the four new ones appended at the end where the roll order puts them.",
